// This is the importer's SECOND door for the same upstream subtyping check: the
// coercion happens at a `let` with an annotated fn-pointer type instead of at a
// call argument. Upstream has no such line — the door is ours, declared below
// rather than hidden — and the pair `--fn-subtyping` / `--c30-let-binding-fnptr`
// exists to ask whether the two coercion SITES behave alike. They do: one fix at
// `subtype()`'s cross-kind early exit closed both on the same build, which is the
// evidence that this is ONE mechanism and not two.
// Original path: tests/ui/regions/regions-fn-subtyping-return-static-fail.rs
